src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:65:An Amendment is a new or proposed change to a ledger rule. Ledger rules affect
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:68:different results. Amendments can be almost anything but they must be accepted
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:69:by a network majority through a consensus process before they are utilized. An
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:70:Amendment must receive at least an 80% approval rate from validating nodes for
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:72:process of an Amendment from its conception to approval and usage.
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:78:- Some members contribute their time and work to develop the Amendment.
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:85:- If the Amendment holds an 80% majority for a two week period, nodes will begin
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:88:Nodes may veto Amendments they consider undesirable by never announcing their
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:89:support for those Amendments. Just a few nodes vetoing an Amendment will normally
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:90:keep it from being accepted. Nodes could also vote yes on an Amendments even
src/xrpld/app/misc/README.md:91:before it obtains a super-majority. This might make sense for a critical bug fix.
